github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6239#issuecomment-5534690526","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSeTR3w","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Custom provider hook bypassed <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Passing <b><i>self.untag</i></b> as <b><i>object_hook</i></b> prevents custom JSON providers from installing their own\n>object hook, so provider-specific values remain undecoded during tagged or session deserialization.\n>Providers backed by libraries that do not accept Python&#x27;s <b><i>object_hook</i></b> keyword may instead fail\n>every load with an exception.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/json/tag.py[315]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6239/files#diff-809a1a0be75dbb211a5a290f9cac295c7703138d9ebd9fc79777cd228865dac9R315-R315)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+        return loads(value, object_hook=self.untag)\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Flask&#x27;s top-level <b><i>loads</i></b> delegates all keyword arguments to <b><i>current_app.json.loads</i></b>, and providers\n>are explicitly customizable or may use other JSON libraries. The repository&#x27;s own custom-provider\n>example installs its hook with <b><i>kwargs.setdefault(&quot;object_hook&quot;, self.object_hook)</i></b>; because the\n>changed line already supplies that key, the provider hook is no longer installed. This serializer is\n>also the default secure-cookie session serializer, extending the regression to session loading.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/json/tag.py[313-315]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/e0914ed00088f068b79928735ef3b9a44fff35a2/src/flask/json/tag.py/#L313-L315)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/json/__init__.py[77-105]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/e0914ed00088f068b79928735ef3b9a44fff35a2/src/flask/json/__init__.py/#L77-L105)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/json/provider.py[19-30]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/e0914ed00088f068b79928735ef3b9a44fff35a2/src/flask/json/provider.py/#L19-L30)</code>\n> <code>[tests/test_json.py[234-243]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/e0914ed00088f068b79928735ef3b9a44fff35a2/tests/test_json.py/#L234-L243)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/sessions.py[273-300]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/e0914ed00088f068b79928735ef3b9a44fff35a2/src/flask/sessions.py/#L273-L300)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>`TaggedJSONSerializer.loads` now passes `object_hook=self.untag` through Flask's configurable JSON provider. This overrides provider-defined hooks and may pass an unsupported Python-specific keyword to alternate JSON implementations.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>Previously, the provider completed its normal deserialization before tagged dictionaries were recursively converted. Preserve that ordering and avoid requiring custom providers to support or compose an `object_hook` argument.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/json/tag.py[297-315]\n>- src/flask/json/__init__.py[77-105]\n>- tests/test_json.py[223-245]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code></div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can route each action level your way: inline, summary, both, or drop</pre>\n\n<a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/tips-and-tricks\">More tips ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://app.qodo.ai/configurations?tab=display-preferences\">Customize Qodo ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai\">Qodo docs ↗</a>\n\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:end -->\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/commit/e0914ed00088f068b79928735ef3b9a44fff35a2 -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","createdAt":"2026-09-04T02:13:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6239#issuecomment-5534699999","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-09-04T02:04:12Z","authors":[{"email":"seonho12-54@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOD8-iGg","login":"seonho12-54","name":"seonho12-54"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-04T02:04:12Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Simplify tagged JSON loading","oid":"e0914ed00088f068b79928735ef3b9a44fff35a2"}],"createdAt":"2026-09-04T02:04:52Z","deletions":13,"files":[